      "title": "Black-clad protesters in balaclavas block road at port of Dover in Kent",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/05/black-clad-protesters-balaclavas-block-road-port-of-dover-kent",
      "description": "<p>Port authorities say access roads ‘free flowing’ again after large group forces road closures in both directions</p><p>Dozens of people dressed in black and wearing balaclavas blocked the road at the port of Dover in Kent, forcing closures in both directions on Saturday morning.</p><p>Kent police said they were were in attendance and engaging with the protest, which the Port of Dover described as a “public order incident”. No arrests were made during the incident. Responsibility for the demonstration appears to have been claimed by an anti-immigration group with links to the far right.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/05/black-clad-protesters-balaclavas-block-road-port-of-dover-kent\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-05T12:20:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Stop the boats’ masked protesters block England’s Port of Dover",
